{
  "_comment": [
    "Sophos Central SIEM v1 — /siem/v1/events. Stream HETEROGENEO: um unico feed",
    "carrega deteccao de malware/PUA, bloqueio de aplicacao e de periferico,",
    "violacao de web control, resultado de update, scan concluido, conectividade",
    "de firewall e sincronismo de AD.",
    "",
    "A VERSAO ANTERIOR CARIMBAVA class_uid=0 EM 100% DO STREAM, com a",
    "justificativa de que 'uma MappingDefinition carrega UM class_uid'. Essa",
    "premissa e FALSA: class_uid e uma regra como qualquer outra e aceita",
    "value_map, entao a classe pode ser decidida POR EVENTO. O custo do erro foi",
    "medido: deteccao de PUA (Event::Endpoint::CorePuaDetection, severity medium)",
    "aterrissava no destino como Base Event, invisivel para toda regra e todo",
    "painel que filtra por Detection Finding.",
    "",
    "POR QUE A CHAVE E `group` E NAO `type`. Os dois estao no evento. `type` e",
    "preciso e INSTAVEL: e uma lista aberta de ~100 valores que a Sophos aumenta",
    "sem aviso, e o modo de falha de uma chave que falta e cair no default em",
    "silencio. `group` e um enum curto (as amostras de producao mostram",
    "PROTECTION, UPDATING, PUA, APPLICATION_CONTROL, WEB, PERIPHERALS,",
    "CONNECTIVITY, AD_SYNC) e muda em ordens de grandeza menos. Sobre 150 eventos",
    "reais de dois tenants, `group` classificou 100% corretamente, incluindo tipos",
    "que NAO estavam em nenhum mapa por `type`.",
    "",
    "ONDE ISTO AINDA PODE FICAR PARA TRAS: um `group` novo de seguranca cai em",
    "Base Event, em silencio. O censo custa uma consulta, porque o grupo cru vai",
    "preservado em unmapped.event_group:",
    "  SELECT unmapped.event_group, count() WHERE class_uid = 0 GROUP BY 1",
    "Um grupo de seguranca aparecendo ai e um membro que falta no value_map.",
    "",
    "class_uid/activity_id/type_uid usam a MESMA chave de proposito: a identidade",
    "type_uid == class_uid*100 + activity_id precisa valer evento a evento, e",
    "mapas com chaves divergentes sao a maneira mais facil de quebra-la. Ha teste",
    "que verifica a identidade sobre fixtures de producao."
  ],
  "rules": [
    {
      "_comment": "GRUPOS DE FINDING. Fora desta lista o evento e telemetria e fica em Base Event (0), que e o fallback OFICIAL do OCSF para log heterogeneo.",
      "target": "normalized.class_uid",
      "source": "group",
      "value_map": {
        "MALWARE": 2004,
        "PUA": 2004,
        "APPLICATION_CONTROL": 2004,
        "WEB": 2004,
        "PERIPHERALS": 2004,
        "DATA_LOSS_PREVENTION": 2004,
        "RUNTIME_DETECTIONS": 2004
      },
      "default": 0,
      "required": true
    },
    {
      "target": "normalized.class_name",
      "source": "group",
      "value_map": {
        "MALWARE": "Detection Finding",
        "PUA": "Detection Finding",
        "APPLICATION_CONTROL": "Detection Finding",
        "WEB": "Detection Finding",
        "PERIPHERALS": "Detection Finding",
        "DATA_LOSS_PREVENTION": "Detection Finding",
        "RUNTIME_DETECTIONS": "Detection Finding"
      },
      "default": "Base Event"
    },
    {
      "target": "normalized.category_uid",
      "source": "group",
      "value_map": {
        "MALWARE": 2,
        "PUA": 2,
        "APPLICATION_CONTROL": 2,
        "WEB": 2,
        "PERIPHERALS": 2,
        "DATA_LOSS_PREVENTION": 2,
        "RUNTIME_DETECTIONS": 2
      },
      "default": 0,
      "required": true
    },
    {
      "target": "normalized.category_name",
      "source": "group",
      "value_map": {
        "MALWARE": "Findings",
        "PUA": "Findings",
        "APPLICATION_CONTROL": "Findings",
        "WEB": "Findings",
        "PERIPHERALS": "Findings",
        "DATA_LOSS_PREVENTION": "Findings",
        "RUNTIME_DETECTIONS": "Findings"
      },
      "default": "Uncategorized"
    },
    {
      "_comment": "1 = Create. O feed SIEM entrega o evento uma vez, no momento em que acontece; nao ha ciclo de vida (Update/Close) como no stream de alert.",
      "target": "normalized.activity_id",
      "source": "group",
      "value_map": {
        "MALWARE": 1,
        "PUA": 1,
        "APPLICATION_CONTROL": 1,
        "WEB": 1,
        "PERIPHERALS": 1,
        "DATA_LOSS_PREVENTION": 1,
        "RUNTIME_DETECTIONS": 1
      },
      "default": 0,
      "required": true
    },
    {
      "target": "normalized.activity_name",
      "source": "group",
      "value_map": {
        "MALWARE": "Create",
        "PUA": "Create",
        "APPLICATION_CONTROL": "Create",
        "WEB": "Create",
        "PERIPHERALS": "Create",
        "DATA_LOSS_PREVENTION": "Create",
        "RUNTIME_DETECTIONS": "Create"
      },
      "default": "Unknown"
    },
    {
      "_comment": "type_uid = class_uid*100 + activity_id: 2004*100+1 = 200401; 0*100+0 = 0.",
      "target": "normalized.type_uid",
      "source": "group",
      "value_map": {
        "MALWARE": 200401,
        "PUA": 200401,
        "APPLICATION_CONTROL": 200401,
        "WEB": 200401,
        "PERIPHERALS": 200401,
        "DATA_LOSS_PREVENTION": 200401,
        "RUNTIME_DETECTIONS": 200401
      },
      "default": 0,
      "required": true
    },

    {
      "target": "normalized.time",
      "source": "created_at || when",
      "type_cast": "iso_to_epoch",
      "required": true
    },
    {
      "target": "normalized.metadata.original_time",
      "source": "when || created_at",
      "default": null
    },
    { "target": "normalized.metadata.version", "const": "1.8.0" },
    { "target": "normalized.metadata.product.name", "const": "Sophos Central" },
    { "target": "normalized.metadata.product.vendor_name", "const": "Sophos" },
    { "target": "normalized.metadata.log_name", "const": "siem/v1/events" },
    { "target": "normalized.metadata.uid", "source": "id", "default": null },
    {
      "_comment": "Sem event_code nada a jusante distingue um tipo de siem_event de outro: `group` decide a CLASSE, mas so o `type` diz qual evento foi.",
      "target": "normalized.metadata.event_code",
      "source": "type",
      "default": null
    },

    {
      "_comment": "enum fechado do schema oficial: NONE|LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH|CRITICAL (pre_cast lowercase)",
      "target": "normalized.severity_id",
      "source": "severity",
      "pre_cast": "lowercase",
      "value_map": {
        "critical": 5,
        "high": 4,
        "medium": 3,
        "low": 2,
        "none": 1
      },
      "default": 0,
      "required": true
    },
    { "target": "normalized.severity", "source": "severity", "default": null },
    { "target": "normalized.message", "source": "name || type", "default": null },

    {
      "_comment": "finding_info e content-required da 2004. Emitido para TODO evento (inclusive Base Event) de proposito: o custo e um objeto pequeno, e a alternativa — emitir so quando a classe e 2004 — nao e expressavel numa regra e produziria finding sem titulo no dia em que um grupo novo entrar no mapa.",
      "target": "normalized.finding_info.title",
      "source": "name",
      "fallback_source": ["type"],
      "default": "Sophos SIEM Event",
      "required": true
    },
    { "target": "normalized.finding_info.uid", "source": "id", "default": null },
    { "target": "normalized.finding_info.desc", "source": "name", "default": null },
    {
      "target": "normalized.finding_info.created_time",
      "source": "created_at",
      "type_cast": "iso_to_epoch",
      "default": null
    },

    {
      "_comment": "3 = Suppressed no enum de finding.json: o produto VIU e NAO bloqueou.",
      "target": "normalized.status_id",
      "source": "type",
      "value_map": {
        "Event::Endpoint::Device::AlertedOnly": 3,
        "Event::Endpoint::Application::Allowed": 3,
        "Event::Endpoint::DataLossPreventionUserAllowed": 3
      },
      "default": null
    },
    {
      "_comment": "1 = Allowed, 2 = Blocked. Miss aqui e inofensivo (null), diferente de class_uid — por isso este mapa pode ser por `type`, que e mais preciso.",
      "target": "normalized.disposition_id",
      "source": "type",
      "value_map": {
        "Event::Endpoint::Application::Blocked": 2,
        "Event::Endpoint::Device::Blocked": 2,
        "Event::Endpoint::WebFilteringBlocked": 2,
        "Event::Endpoint::Threat::CleanedUp": 2,
        "Event::Endpoint::Device::AlertedOnly": 1,
        "Event::Endpoint::Application::Allowed": 1,
        "Event::Endpoint::DataLossPreventionUserAllowed": 1
      },
      "default": null
    },

    { "target": "normalized.device.uid", "source": "endpoint_id", "default": null },
    { "target": "normalized.device.type", "source": "endpoint_type", "default": null },
    {
      "target": "normalized.device.type_id",
      "source": "endpoint_type",
      "pre_cast": "lowercase",
      "value_map": {
        "computer": 1,
        "server": 2,
        "mobile": 3,
        "securityappliance": 4
      },
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "_comment": "`location` NAO e sempre hostname: na familia Event::Firewall::* ele carrega o SERIAL do appliance, e hostname_t so aceita hostname. So aceita `location` quando ha endpoint_id (evento de endpoint).",
      "target": "normalized.device.hostname",
      "source": "[endpoint_id && location][?@!=null && @!=`false`] | [0]",
      "default": null
    },
    {
      "_comment": "O outro lado da mesma regra: sem endpoint_id, `location` e o serial do appliance.",
      "target": "normalized.device.serial_number",
      "source": "[(!endpoint_id) && location][?@!=null && @!=`false`] | [0]",
      "default": null
    },
    {
      "_comment": "source_info e mapa livre string->string; 'ip' e a chave usual mas nao e garantida pelo schema",
      "target": "normalized.device.ip",
      "source": "source_info.ip",
      "default": null
    },
    { "target": "normalized.actor.user.name", "source": "source", "default": null },
    { "target": "normalized.actor.user.uid", "source": "user_id", "default": null },
    { "target": "normalized.cloud.org.uid", "source": "customer_id", "default": null },
    { "target": "normalized.cloud.provider", "const": "Sophos Central" },

    { "target": "normalized.unmapped.event_type", "source": "type", "default": null },
    {
      "_comment": "A chave da classificacao vai preservada crua: e o que permite auditar o value_map de class_uid direto no destino.",
      "target": "normalized.unmapped.event_group",
      "source": "group",
      "default": null
    },
    { "target": "normalized.unmapped.threat", "source": "threat", "default": null },
    { "target": "normalized.unmapped.origin", "source": "origin", "default": null },
    { "target": "normalized.unmapped.app_sha256", "source": "appSha256", "default": null },
    { "target": "normalized.unmapped.app_certs", "source": "appCerts", "default": null },
    {
      "_comment": "objeto {items:[{descriptor,result,type}], totalItems:int} — NAO e array",
      "target": "normalized.unmapped.core_remedy_items",
      "source": "core_remedy_items.items",
      "default": null
    },
    {
      "target": "normalized.unmapped.core_remedy_total",
      "source": "core_remedy_items.totalItems",
      "default": null
    },
    { "target": "normalized.unmapped.ips_threat_data", "source": "ips_threat_data", "default": null },
    { "target": "normalized.unmapped.amsi_threat_data", "source": "amsi_threat_data", "default": null },
    {
      "_comment": "array de {property,type} com enum de ~25 tipos (IPS_*, AMSI_*, HMPA_*, CORE_EVENT_*)",
      "target": "normalized.unmapped.details",
      "source": "details",
      "default": null
    },
    {
      "target": "normalized.unmapped.whitelist_properties",
      "source": "whitelist_properties",
      "default": null
    },
    {
      "_comment": "mapa livre string->string no schema; a chave depende do tipo de evento",
      "target": "normalized.unmapped.source_info",
      "source": "source_info",
      "default": null
    },

    {
      "target": "normalized.observables",
      "kind": "array_builder",
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "device.uid",
          "type": "Endpoint",
          "type_id": 20,
          "source": "endpoint_id",
          "skip_null": true
        },
        {
          "name": "device.hostname",
          "type": "Hostname",
          "type_id": 1,
          "source": "[endpoint_id && location][?@!=null && @!=`false`] | [0]",
          "skip_null": true
        },
        {
          "name": "device.ip",
          "type": "IP Address",
          "type_id": 2,
          "source": "source_info.ip",
          "skip_null": true
        },
        {
          "name": "actor.user.name",
          "type": "User Name",
          "type_id": 4,
          "source": "source",
          "skip_null": true
        },
        {
          "name": "unmapped.app_sha256",
          "type": "Hash",
          "type_id": 8,
          "source": "appSha256",
          "skip_null": true
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "raw_reduction": [
    { "path": "core_remedy_items.items", "max_items": 20 },
    { "path": "details", "max_items": 30 },
    { "path": "whitelist_properties", "max_items": 20 },
    { "path": "ips_threat_data.rawData", "max_bytes": 4096 }
  ]
}
